*
!private/
!public/
!.gitignore

# The two .gitkeep files have to be re-included here rather than in the root
# .gitignore. Git gives the deepest matching ignore file the last word, so the
# `*` above beats a negation written higher up, and without these lines a fresh
# clone has no storage/app/public directory for uploads to land in.
!private/.gitkeep
!public/.gitkeep
